# Generative AI Course Practice Code

This repository contains my personal practice code and notes based on the course materials from:

**T81-559: Applications of Generative Artificial Intelligence**  
Instructor: Jeff Heaton  
Original course repository: https://github.com/jeffheaton/app_generative_ai

## Purpose

The goal of this repository is to organize and run course-related code independently.  
The materials focus on practical applications of Generative AI, including OpenAI API usage, LangChain, prompt engineering, RAG, agents, multimodal models, image generation, fine-tuning, and Streamlit applications.

## Topics Covered

- Introduction to Generative AI
- OpenAI API usage
- Prompt engineering
- LangChain basics
- Chat memory and persistence
- Output parsers and structured responses
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
- Embeddings and vector databases
- Agents and tools
- Kaggle and small LLM workflows
- Image generation and multimodal AI
- Streamlit-based AI applications
- Fine-tuning and evaluation
- Speech-to-text and text-to-speech applications